1 NOTE {geni:about_me} CHRISTIERSON, Frank von. b. Lovisa, near Helsinki, Finland, 25 December 1900; d. Roseville, California, 24 April 1996. Von Christierson came to the USA with his family in 1905. He was educated at Stanford Universit
2 CONC y (BA 1923), and San Francisco Theological Seminary (BD 1929, MA 1930). He was ordained a Presbyterian minister in 1929, and served at Calvary Presbyterian Church in Berkeley, California (1930-44); Trinity Presbyterian Church in N
2 CONC orth Hollywood (1944-61); and Celtic Cross Church in Citrus Heights (1961-65). He served several times as moderator of regional Presbyterian assemblies, and continued assisting various congregations in California and Nevada during
2 CONC  his retirement. In 1983 he was awarded the citation of distinguished alumnus, and became a Fellow of The Hymn Society.  He has published a hymnal collection entitled Make a Joyful Noise (1987) and is represented in many hymnals. 
2 CONC Three of his hymn texts have been included in the new Hope hymnal Worship & Rejoice (2001). 
