1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Selma Ottilia Lovisa Lagerlöf==
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selma_Lagerl%C3%B6f '''Selma Ottilia Lovisa Lagerlöf'''] was a Swedish author and teacher. She published her first novel, Gösta Berling's Saga, at the age of 33. She was the first Swede, and the first
2 CONC  woman to win the Nobel Prize in Literature which she was awarded in 1909. Additionally, she was the first woman to be granted a membership in The Swedish Academy.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://nobelprize.org/nobel_prizes/literature/laureates/1909/lagerlof-bio.html The Nobel Prize in Literature 1909]: "in appreciation of the lofty idealism, vivid imagination and spiritual perception that characterize her writings
2 CONC "
2 CONT
2 CONT Swedish:
2 CONT * Historiesajten - [http://www.historiesajten.se/visainfo.asp?id=308 Selma Lagerlöf.]
2 CONT * Svenskt Biografiskt Lexikon - [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=10922 Selma O L Lagerlöf.]
2 CONT * Wikipedia: [http://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selma_Lagerl%C3%B6f Selma Lagerlöf.] 
2 CONT * Nääs Slott: [http://www.naas.se/slottet/historien/sophie-elkan-selma-lagerloef/ Sophie Elkan och Selma Lagerlöf]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT När Selma var 9 år fick hon bo hos sin morbror och moster Oriel Afzelius o Maria Wallroth i Stockholm. Hon bodde hos dem för att hon skulle gå på ett gymnastik institut, något som hon hade blivit ordinerad för sitt onda ben. Famil
2 CONC jen Afzelius bodde då Selma var hos dem på Klara strand gatan 7 i Stockholm.
